+
+`node test/riscv/run.cjs` bundles the tests with esbuild and runs them under node.
+
+- `disasm.test.ts`: 60,847 encodings × 4 objdump variants (default, `-M numeric`, `-M no-aliases`, both), plus 6 format-wrapper cases. That is 237,078 checks with 0 failures.
+  - The expected text comes from GNU objdump 2.43.1 (a RISC-V GNU toolchain; `make_expected.sh` takes its bin folder from `RISCV_BIN`) run over `corpus.s`.
+  - The corpus has 99 hand-picked encodings, one per alias rule, and 3,000 random RV32IMC/Zicsr encodings (seeded). Added after review: all 4096 CSR numbers, 300 fences with random rd/rs1/fm, 150 fully random words for each 32-bit major opcode, and all 49,152 16-bit compressed encodings.
+  - `gen_corpus.py` and `make_expected.sh` regenerate them. 91,688 of the checks are encodings that both objdump and this disassembler call unknown. 6,316 are the RV32-reserved shifts, which are expected to show as hex.
+- `alias.test.ts`: 82 checks covering every syntax form above, plus regressions for review findings M1, M2, M4, L3-L9, N2-N4 and `.rc` handling. The alias files in it were written for the test.
+- End to end in WKWebView (`../www-instr`, `?selftest=1`, invisible harness `src/wk-snapshot-hidden.swift`): VS Code's undo/redo stack (from `document.ts`) is emulated in host.js. 19 checks, all passing.
+  - Loading bindings makes exactly one User update. A user override survives `add-variable`. A newly added bound row is bound with no extra undo step. Undo removes it and keeps the restored formats. A second undo restores the bound format. The redo stack survives, and redo works.
+  - After the viewer empties (rowIds restart), a re-added row is bound again. `R&W<1>` displays as text. After `clearValueAliases` and a load with `apply:false`, adding a signal binds only the new row (N1). No "Unknown webview message type" logs.
+  - The same self-test (its first 17 checks) against the a396e12 build fails 6 of them (H1, the add-variable undo checks and L2).
+- `npx tsc -p tsconfig.webview.json --noEmit` is clean. `node esbuild.js` builds.
